[[2047,127,0,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>The supply for module \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E63</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               arrives\ndirectly from the battery. (maxifuse J/B1 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B99</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ) to pin\n1 via fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of junction unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B1</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ; the supply controlled\nby the ignition (INT) reaches pin 3 of the line protected by fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F4</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of\nthe additional fuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98B</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>Pin 11 is earthed.</p><p>The control buttons, incorporated in the\nclimate control system \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M70</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               controls, are connected to pins\n16, 19 and 20. A serial line also connects module \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E63</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               - from\npin 13- to the climate control system \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M70</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The SET button, located in the steering\ncolumn switch unit (\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H5</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              connector E) is connected to pin 15.</p><p>Pins 4, 8, 5 and 9 of instrument \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E63</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               are\nconnected to the switches at the locks of the front doors (connector\nC of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N50</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N51</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ) and the rear doors (connector B\nof \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N55</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N56</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ), respectively and signal if any of\nthe doors is open. Similarly, the opening of the boot is signalled\nby switch \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>I11</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               to pin 6.</p><p>The signal indicating the operation of the\ninertia switch \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>I50</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               reaches pin 10 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E63</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>A serial line connects module \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E63, from\npin 7, with speedometer module E10 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 See\n\t\tE4021\n\t\tSPEEDOMETER\n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 with this\nline used to send information concerning the warning lights (for\nthe repetition of the signal at the actual INFOCENTER) for the engine\noil level, speedometer signal, etc.</strong></p><p>The engine temperature signal is sent again\nat pin 17 to module \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E20</strong><a href=\"#/3234358\">E4023</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The engine oil pressure signal is sent again\nat pin 18 to module \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E30</strong><a href=\"#/3234338\">E4022</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>Module \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E63</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               has its own diagnostic\nserial line - from pins 2 and 12 - which is connected to a specific\ndiagnostic socket, \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>R57</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><h3>Functional description</h3><p>The oil temperature sensor\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K29</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              provides\na signal at pin 14 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E63</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               for display purposes.</p>"]]